1
00:00:17,120 --> 00:00:24,460
We sigh whenever we're about to come to a standstill

2
00:00:17,120 --> 00:00:24,460
Owarinaki tabi no tochuu tachidomarisouna toki

3
00:00:24,460 --> 00:00:30,710
While moving on this endless journey.

4
00:00:24,460 --> 00:00:30,710
Fukai tameiki kobosu bokura wa

5
00:00:32,800 --> 00:00:38,430
Everytime we lunge for it, it escapes and flies off.

6
00:00:32,800 --> 00:00:38,430
Tsukamikaketewa mata hanareteitta

7
00:00:38,890 --> 00:00:45,850
But now, there's nothing to be afraid of

8
00:00:38,890 --> 00:00:45,850
Demo ima wa mou nanimo osoreru koto wa nai

9
00:00:46,480 --> 00:00:53,780
The powerful ties that bind our hearts

10
00:00:46,480 --> 00:00:53,780
Kokoro wo tsunagu tsuyoi kizuna wa

11
00:00:53,780 --> 00:00:59,240
Will never come loose.

12
00:00:53,780 --> 00:00:59,240
Keshite hodoke wa shinai sa

13
00:01:01,280 --> 00:01:08,960
After a lifetime of searching, we finally arrived

14
00:01:01,280 --> 00:01:08,960
Sagashitsuzukete tadoritsuita

15
00:01:08,960 --> 00:01:14,760
Here, where the period lies.

16
00:01:08,960 --> 00:01:14,760
Kono basho de piriodo ni

17
00:01:15,920 --> 00:01:24,060
Let's change all our sorrow and rage to power.

18
00:01:15,920 --> 00:01:24,060
Kanashimi ikari chikara ni kaete

19
00:01:24,060 --> 00:01:28,980
Destiny is right within our reach.

20
00:01:24,060 --> 00:01:28,980
Unmei wa sugu soba ni

21
00:01:33,360 --> 00:01:36,150
On the day before the Promised Day,

22
00:01:36,150 --> 00:01:39,990
Alphonse Elric lies dormant in the Eastern training grounds.

23
00:01:41,410 --> 00:01:48,540
However, he is captured by the sudden appearances of the Homunculi, Gluttony and Pride.

24
00:01:57,800 --> 00:01:59,010
Alphonse...

25
00:02:04,220 --> 00:02:06,100
Pick yourself up...

26
00:02:06,100 --> 00:02:07,390
Alphonse...

27
00:02:09,730 --> 00:02:10,600
Who...

28
00:02:14,860 --> 00:02:17,030
It's far too early for you to die.

29
00:02:17,820 --> 00:02:23,490
I still have plenty of things for you to do.

30
00:02:24,560 --> 00:02:27,560
Emissary of Darkness

31
00:02:24,560 --> 00:02:27,560
Emissary of Darkness

32
00:02:43,390 --> 00:02:45,010
Excuse me...

33
00:02:45,010 --> 00:02:46,760
Are we in Kanama?

34
00:02:50,980 --> 00:02:52,060
Mr. Hoh!

35
00:02:53,400 --> 00:02:54,520
You've got some visitors.

36
00:03:01,490 --> 00:03:03,490
So you're here, Edwa-

37
00:03:04,910 --> 00:03:07,410
God, that felt good.

38
00:03:07,410 --> 00:03:10,370
The first thing you do is punch me in the face?!

39
00:03:10,370 --> 00:03:12,000
And with your right hand, too!

40
00:03:13,750 --> 00:03:15,840
Looks like you made some new friends.

41
00:03:15,840 --> 00:03:16,170
Fri-

42
00:03:16,170 --> 00:03:19,170
We're just working with him due to the circumstances.

43
00:03:19,170 --> 00:03:21,880
And I'm the boss of all of them.

44
00:03:23,380 --> 00:03:25,550
Oh my.

45
00:03:25,550 --> 00:03:28,010
Thank you for taking care of my son.

46
00:03:28,010 --> 00:03:29,180
Not a problem.

47
00:03:29,180 --> 00:03:31,560
Though he's one hell of a brat.

48
00:03:31,560 --> 00:03:32,270
Shut up!

49
00:03:33,770 --> 00:03:35,770
Interesting tattoo you've got there.

50
00:03:37,190 --> 00:03:37,900
Oh.

51
00:03:38,440 --> 00:03:39,440
This.

52
00:03:40,690 --> 00:03:42,530
Guess there's no point in hiding it.

53
00:03:44,110 --> 00:03:46,490
You'd better not hide anything either, old man.

54
00:03:50,290 --> 00:03:53,210
Tomorrow is the "Promised Day", right?

55
00:03:56,210 --> 00:03:57,210
Yeah.

56
00:03:57,920 --> 00:03:59,880
I'll tell you guys everything.

57
00:04:15,100 --> 00:04:19,900
Guess you won't be able to accept it as easily as Alphonse did.

58
00:04:19,900 --> 00:04:21,280
You told Al too?!

59
00:04:22,070 --> 00:04:23,110
Yeah.

60
00:04:23,110 --> 00:04:27,910
He probably has a lot to think about, but he accepted it.

61
00:04:31,830 --> 00:04:34,710
The philosopher's stone you've been looking for is right here.

62
00:04:34,710 --> 00:04:35,540
Do you want to use it?

63
00:04:35,790 --> 00:04:37,380
Don't fuck with me!

64
00:04:37,380 --> 00:04:39,630
They're lives of people who are totally uninvolved!

65
00:04:39,630 --> 00:04:42,260
We lost our bodies due to our own carelessness!

66
00:04:42,260 --> 00:04:43,420
What gives us the right to use their lives?!

67
00:04:46,340 --> 00:04:48,680
I'm glad my son grew up to say that.

68
00:04:52,430 --> 00:04:55,270
A solar eclipse occurs tomorrow.

69
00:04:55,270 --> 00:04:57,350
He's planning on using that.

70
00:04:57,650 --> 00:04:59,020
A solar eclipse?

71
00:04:59,020 --> 00:05:00,360
How would he use that?

72
00:05:00,980 --> 00:05:02,110
Edward.

73
00:05:03,030 --> 00:05:06,700
Would you be willing to help me stop his plans?

74
00:05:06,700 --> 00:05:08,490
'Help'?!

75
00:05:08,490 --> 00:05:10,030
Don't get the wrong idea!

76
00:05:10,030 --> 00:05:14,200
I'm going to beat the hell out of that geezer even if I don't  have to work with you!

77
00:05:14,450 --> 00:05:19,920
I'm just listening to what you have to say right now because teaming up with you might increase our odds of 	winning!

78
00:05:27,760 --> 00:05:29,430
I'm glad to hear...

79
00:05:29,430 --> 00:05:33,720
Whatever the reason may be, you're willing to fight alongside me.

80
00:05:39,730 --> 00:05:43,400
Granny Pinako asked me to tell you Mom's last words.

81
00:05:47,490 --> 00:05:49,660
"Sorry I couldn't keep my promise."

82
00:05:51,160 --> 00:05:52,700
"I'm going to have to leave you first."

83
00:05:59,210 --> 00:06:00,880
Message delivered!

84
00:06:18,640 --> 00:06:23,810
Hey, shouldn't you try to sit knee to knee with your father and open up to him?

85
00:06:23,810 --> 00:06:24,980
Yeah, man.

86
00:06:24,980 --> 00:06:26,900
You should at least call him "Old Man".

87
00:06:27,530 --> 00:06:29,820
Seems like a lot happened in the past,

88
00:06:29,820 --> 00:06:33,030
but he definitely doesn't seem like someone who would abandon his wife.

89
00:06:33,700 --> 00:06:36,040
He probably has a lot of personal reasons.

90
00:06:36,040 --> 00:06:38,700
Come on. Listen to what he has to say.

91
00:06:38,700 --> 00:06:40,660
Shut up already!

92
00:06:40,660 --> 00:06:42,920
I've got a lot of personal reasons, too!

93
00:06:42,920 --> 00:06:44,500
For example?

94
00:06:44,500 --> 00:06:46,380
You're probably just too stubborn and proud.

95
00:06:48,130 --> 00:06:50,590
You can't organize your thoughts very well, right?

96
00:06:51,680 --> 00:06:53,140
Can't really blame you.

97
00:06:53,140 --> 00:06:56,260
He's a philosopher's stone in the shape of a human.

98
00:06:56,260 --> 00:06:59,980
To top it off, he's also your dad.

99
00:07:00,770 --> 00:07:02,480
That's not all of it.

100
00:07:04,770 --> 00:07:07,980
He just showed a side of himself that I wasn't really expecting.

101
00:07:18,580 --> 00:07:22,620
You know... someday, I'll turn into a wrinkled old woman who looks like a monster.

102
00:07:23,580 --> 00:07:28,630
But no matter how I end up looking, I'll always be happy to take a picture with the family where everyone is 	smiling.

103
00:07:29,170 --> 00:07:31,470
So please... stay with your family.

104
00:07:32,930 --> 00:07:35,890
Trisha, I'm going.

105
00:07:36,760 --> 00:07:38,180
Please wait for me.

106
00:07:46,520 --> 00:07:47,270
Okay.

107
00:07:51,740 --> 00:07:53,070
I'll be waiting.

108
00:07:59,080 --> 00:08:02,910
"Sorry I couldn't keep my promise."

109
00:08:04,330 --> 00:08:06,330
"I'm going to have to leave you first.", huh...

110
00:08:08,130 --> 00:08:11,340
Even though we couldn't age and die together,

111
00:08:11,920 --> 00:08:16,680
you must believe from the bottom of your heart that I'll come after you in the future.

112
00:08:20,560 --> 00:08:23,310
It'll be tomorrow... Trisha.

113
00:08:27,480 --> 00:08:28,980
Here you go.

114
00:08:28,980 --> 00:08:30,570
Thanks.

115
00:08:30,570 --> 00:08:32,530
What are you going to do with that?

116
00:08:41,910 --> 00:08:44,330
You're going to wear something flashy like this again?

117
00:08:44,330 --> 00:08:46,040
Why's it gotta be red?

118
00:08:50,590 --> 00:08:54,510
This is probably going to be our last battle against them.

119
00:08:55,380 --> 00:08:57,180
I'm going to need to be psyched.

120
00:09:01,510 --> 00:09:02,970
Hey, you know...

121
00:09:02,970 --> 00:09:06,440
You don't really have to stick with me through all of this.

122
00:09:06,440 --> 00:09:10,480
I personally think it would be better for you guys if you were to leave to attend to your own business from 		here.

123
00:09:10,810 --> 00:09:14,360
Hey, you're one of my henchmen. Don't go ordering me around.

124
00:09:14,360 --> 00:09:18,240
I guess you guys want to return to your original bodies too?

125
00:09:18,240 --> 00:09:19,660
I wonder...

126
00:09:19,660 --> 00:09:24,370
This body can be pretty convenient.
I guess I wouldn't mind staying like this forever.

127
00:09:25,750 --> 00:09:27,120
That's the spirit!

128
00:09:28,040 --> 00:09:29,500
Then... why?

129
00:09:29,790 --> 00:09:31,500
Well, you know.

130
00:09:31,500 --> 00:09:33,380
We don't really have anywhere else to go.

131
00:09:33,380 --> 00:09:38,010
My animal instincts tell me that I'm better off staying here.

132
00:09:38,300 --> 00:09:39,640
Okay...

133
00:09:40,890 --> 00:09:42,970
And what about you?

134
00:09:42,970 --> 00:09:46,640
Weren't you saying something about running away from the other Homunculi?

135
00:09:47,480 --> 00:09:50,650
You're asking why I came back to Central?

136
00:09:51,190 --> 00:09:52,650
Not tellin'.

137
00:10:00,660 --> 00:10:02,030
What is it?

138
00:10:14,380 --> 00:10:15,380
Al!

139
00:10:16,460 --> 00:10:18,630
Man, don't scare me like that!

140
00:10:19,720 --> 00:10:21,470
I'm glad we were able to join up!

141
00:10:21,470 --> 00:10:22,600
How have you been?

142
00:10:22,600 --> 00:10:25,220
Looks like you were safe and sound too, Brother.

143
00:10:25,220 --> 00:10:28,770
Huh? Aren't you supposed to be with Major Miles?

144
00:10:29,180 --> 00:10:31,020
Is everything going well over there?

145
00:10:31,440 --> 00:10:33,270
I actually wanted to talk to you about that.

146
00:10:33,270 --> 00:10:34,440
Could you come here for a second?

147
00:10:34,440 --> 00:10:35,820
Y-Yeah.

148
00:10:38,860 --> 00:10:41,280
Al... is something wrong?

149
00:10:45,120 --> 00:10:46,660
Why do you ask?

150
00:10:46,660 --> 00:10:48,950
I dunno... I just got a feeling.

151
00:10:48,950 --> 00:10:50,000
Ed!

152
00:10:50,540 --> 00:10:51,460
Lin!

153
00:10:51,460 --> 00:10:52,830
Get away from him!

154
00:10:54,380 --> 00:10:55,250
He's...

155
00:10:57,300 --> 00:10:58,760
That's...!

156
00:11:12,440 --> 00:11:14,270
W-What's going on?!

157
00:11:14,900 --> 00:11:19,150
So you joined them, Greed.

158
00:11:26,830 --> 00:11:30,250
And you were taken control of by a human like that...

159
00:11:32,790 --> 00:11:35,000
Your soul is too weak!

160
00:11:45,550 --> 00:11:48,180
The Führer President is still missing?

161
00:11:48,180 --> 00:11:52,390
Apparently, all they found was the corpse of one of his men downstream.

162
00:11:52,390 --> 00:11:55,310
It would be a miracle if he were to be alive after this.

163
00:11:55,310 --> 00:12:01,070
I'll lead the search team, and I'll also ask the Northern army to lend us a hand.

164
00:12:01,070 --> 00:12:02,820
You're going to step foot on the front lines yourself?

165
00:12:03,360 --> 00:12:08,080
I'll never be able to rest easy until I see his corpse with my own two eyes.

166
00:12:08,780 --> 00:12:12,500
You're not going to target Central as according to your original plan?

167
00:12:12,500 --> 00:12:14,250
Nothing I can do.

168
00:12:14,250 --> 00:12:18,590
I'll just have to hand over the fatty portions of Central to Colonel Mustang.

169
00:12:19,880 --> 00:12:24,590
Currently, the Bradley administration is operating without any trouble.

170
00:12:25,260 --> 00:12:31,390
If Colonel Mustang and Major General Armstrong were to go through with the operation,

171
00:12:31,390 --> 00:12:33,810
they'll probably be treated as rebels.

172
00:12:33,810 --> 00:12:37,600
And when that happens, it'll be my turn to shine.

173
00:12:38,690 --> 00:12:41,440
After they become seen as the villains,

174
00:12:41,440 --> 00:12:46,110
I, Lieutenant General Grumman, the defender of justice, will arrive on the scene.

175
00:12:46,860 --> 00:12:51,580
In order for me to stand at the top of this country with the least amount of risk,

176
00:12:51,580 --> 00:12:55,500
I'm going to need the younglings to pull the chestnuts out of the fire.

177
00:12:56,370 --> 00:13:00,630
That's probably exactly what this raccoon is thinking right now.

178
00:13:02,800 --> 00:13:06,260
I joined forces with him since we're right on the brink of the Promised Day,

179
00:13:07,260 --> 00:13:09,550
but I shouldn't let my guard down until the very end.

180
00:13:19,940 --> 00:13:21,900
A-Al...

181
00:13:21,900 --> 00:13:22,980
It's Pride.

182
00:13:23,820 --> 00:13:25,110
'Pride'?

183
00:13:25,110 --> 00:13:26,700
Yeah.

184
00:13:26,700 --> 00:13:30,490
I guess he's sort of like our eldest brother.

185
00:13:31,530 --> 00:13:32,990
A Homunculus?!

186
00:13:34,830 --> 00:13:38,330
So you're going to betray us no matter what, Greed?

187
00:13:39,080 --> 00:13:43,250
Then at this point, you're nothing but an obstacle for us.

188
00:13:43,250 --> 00:13:44,630
Damn you...

189
00:13:44,630 --> 00:13:46,340
How did you know we were here?!

190
00:13:48,130 --> 00:13:51,510
How dare you transform into Al!

191
00:13:51,510 --> 00:13:53,600
I didn't transform into anything.

192
00:13:56,020 --> 00:13:59,140
This is really your little brother's body.

193
00:14:03,980 --> 00:14:05,780
You son of a...!

194
00:14:06,530 --> 00:14:09,820
I'm going to dispose of Greed right here and now.

195
00:14:09,820 --> 00:14:13,450
And then, I'm going to have the Fullmetal Alchemist come with me afterwards.

196
00:14:16,040 --> 00:14:18,410
Hey! You two should hide somewhere-

197
00:14:18,410 --> 00:14:20,750
Wow, you guys sure didn't waste any time, did you?!

198
00:14:20,750 --> 00:14:24,290
Our animal instincts are telling us not to fight that thing!

199
00:14:26,380 --> 00:14:27,920
Are you going to be okay?

200
00:14:28,380 --> 00:14:30,130
Of course I am.

201
00:14:30,130 --> 00:14:32,850
They can't kill Al and I because they need us for whatever reason.

202
00:14:33,220 --> 00:14:36,270
But on the other hand, I can give them everything I've got!

203
00:14:36,270 --> 00:14:38,140
I'm going to beat you to a pulp!

204
00:14:38,980 --> 00:14:41,810
You're right; I'm not going to kill you.

205
00:14:42,350 --> 00:14:46,400
However, I can't guarantee that you won't lose a limb or three.

206
00:14:53,780 --> 00:14:56,290
I can't escape into the slums!

207
00:15:03,960 --> 00:15:06,590
You can't guard against this guy!

208
00:15:08,340 --> 00:15:09,550
That was close!

209
00:15:14,470 --> 00:15:18,220
Well, I've captured your friend.

210
00:15:18,220 --> 00:15:23,770
Do I also have to capture the people in the slums in order for you to cooperate with me?

211
00:15:25,020 --> 00:15:26,690
He's good.

212
00:15:26,690 --> 00:15:29,860
He's going right for your soft spots.

213
00:15:44,000 --> 00:15:47,500
I can't be on the losing side all the time.

214
00:16:06,900 --> 00:16:07,770
What?

215
00:16:07,770 --> 00:16:08,440
A power outage?

216
00:16:08,440 --> 00:16:09,820
What's going on?!

217
00:16:16,990 --> 00:16:19,080
I can't see anything,

218
00:16:19,080 --> 00:16:20,620
but the eyeballs have also disappeared.

219
00:16:23,540 --> 00:16:24,620
Greed!

220
00:16:24,620 --> 00:16:25,750
Is that you, Heinekel?

221
00:16:26,120 --> 00:16:27,130
What's going on?

222
00:16:27,130 --> 00:16:28,500
What happened?!

223
00:16:28,500 --> 00:16:31,550
A shadow only exists if there is light.

224
00:16:31,550 --> 00:16:34,010
He can't even materialize in the dark,

225
00:16:34,010 --> 00:16:36,680
and can't see anything just like us.

226
00:16:37,180 --> 00:16:38,680
So he left?!

227
00:16:38,680 --> 00:16:40,810
He's just lurking somewhere.

228
00:16:40,810 --> 00:16:43,390
If the lights come back on, he'll be back...

229
00:16:44,140 --> 00:16:45,730
What are we going to do, then?!

230
00:16:46,770 --> 00:16:50,190
Heinekel... did you see Alphonse's shadow earlier?

231
00:16:50,190 --> 00:16:51,190
Yeah.

232
00:16:51,190 --> 00:16:53,530
There were a lot of these tentacles crawling about.

233
00:16:53,530 --> 00:16:54,570
Not that.

234
00:16:54,990 --> 00:16:57,780
He was always near a large shadow, right?

235
00:16:58,820 --> 00:17:01,330
Pride's real body is somewhere within the shadows of the forest.

236
00:17:01,740 --> 00:17:02,790
His real body?!

237
00:17:03,410 --> 00:17:05,410
So it's not in Al's armor?!

238
00:17:05,410 --> 00:17:06,960
Nope.

239
00:17:06,960 --> 00:17:10,670
He has a container just for himself to use whenever he goes out.

240
00:17:11,460 --> 00:17:12,960
What kind of 'container'?

241
00:17:20,430 --> 00:17:22,810
No moon or stars in the sky, huh...

242
00:17:23,850 --> 00:17:27,230
They can't maneuver in this darkness either.

243
00:17:27,940 --> 00:17:30,440
Guess I'll just have to wait for the slums to get their power back...

244
00:17:37,110 --> 00:17:38,450
You're not getting away!

245
00:17:41,320 --> 00:17:44,660
So my child's figure doesn't stop you from attacking me.

246
00:17:44,660 --> 00:17:45,910
You're pretty good.

247
00:17:45,910 --> 00:17:49,540
You're right. I do feel bad for having to kill a child!

248
00:17:51,210 --> 00:17:53,050
But then again,

249
00:17:53,050 --> 00:17:55,420
my animal instincts are overwhelming my conscience!

250
00:17:55,840 --> 00:17:59,010
It's telling me that I have to kill you here and now!

251
00:18:03,260 --> 00:18:04,010
Ed!

252
00:18:05,100 --> 00:18:05,930
Hey, Ed!

253
00:18:06,560 --> 00:18:07,520
Is that you, Donkey Kong?

254
00:18:08,640 --> 00:18:10,060
How's your little brother doing?

255
00:18:10,060 --> 00:18:11,940
He doesn't seem to have moved at all.

256
00:18:11,940 --> 00:18:14,190
You can hear it when he does.

257
00:18:14,690 --> 00:18:17,320
Okay. Let's leave this place for now.

258
00:18:17,320 --> 00:18:18,900
You're telling me to abandon Al?!

259
00:18:19,240 --> 00:18:21,570
I understand that you're worried,

260
00:18:21,570 --> 00:18:23,910
but what if we were to approach him carelessly, just to find that it was a 	trap?

261
00:18:24,870 --> 00:18:30,620
We need to stick together until Heinekel takes care of Pride in order to avoid accidentally attacking each 	other.

262
00:18:34,250 --> 00:18:37,920
Is that... the sound of Lion King fighting?

263
00:18:38,380 --> 00:18:42,390
Let's just leave it to the nocturnals for now.

264
00:18:45,560 --> 00:18:47,060
Damn that Pride...

265
00:18:47,060 --> 00:18:49,770
How did he know we were here?

266
00:18:49,770 --> 00:18:52,020
That shouldn't be a part of his abilities...

267
00:18:57,780 --> 00:18:58,280
Duck!

268
00:19:10,620 --> 00:19:13,880
Smells like the Fullmetal Alchemist.

269
00:19:13,880 --> 00:19:15,790
Smells like Greed.

270
00:19:15,790 --> 00:19:18,000
Judging from the voice... Gluttony?!

271
00:19:18,000 --> 00:19:19,170
Him?!

272
00:19:19,170 --> 00:19:20,720
Now I get it.

273
00:19:20,720 --> 00:19:25,050
He used Gluttony's keen sense of smell to find us.

274
00:19:25,470 --> 00:19:30,680
I also smell a scent of a guy I don't recognize!

275
00:19:30,680 --> 00:19:32,600
I can eat him, right?

276
00:19:33,020 --> 00:19:35,310
He's talking about you, Darius.

277
00:19:35,310 --> 00:19:37,400
That one's also a Homunculus.

278
00:19:37,400 --> 00:19:39,610
How do you expect me to fight against a monster like that?

279
00:19:40,240 --> 00:19:43,490
He's just following his nose.

280
00:19:44,490 --> 00:19:47,700
In this situation, you should be evenly matched.

281
00:19:47,700 --> 00:19:51,500
My animal instincts are telling me not to do it, but...

282
00:19:52,960 --> 00:19:55,080
Men are all about guts!

283
00:19:55,080 --> 00:19:56,750
Victory goes to the swiftest!

284
00:20:04,180 --> 00:20:06,890
One more!

285
00:20:08,930 --> 00:20:11,140
Damn it, Donkey Kong...

286
00:20:11,140 --> 00:20:14,980
I thought we were sticking together to avoid attacking each other...

287
00:20:14,980 --> 00:20:15,690
My bad.

288
00:20:16,310 --> 00:20:20,320
I guess Gluttony will still have the advantage in the dark.

289
00:20:20,320 --> 00:20:22,940
But if we were to turn on the lights, Pride would...

290
00:20:23,950 --> 00:20:25,700
This is troublesome.

291
00:20:26,360 --> 00:20:27,700
Hey, Greed.

292
00:20:28,200 --> 00:20:28,990
That you, Lin?

293
00:20:29,660 --> 00:20:30,830
Switch with me for a sec.

294
00:20:31,410 --> 00:20:34,920
I can sense the aura of the Homunculi.

295
00:20:34,920 --> 00:20:37,080
I was also the one to notice Pride, right?

296
00:20:37,580 --> 00:20:40,710
I can fight better than you in this darkness.

297
00:20:44,130 --> 00:20:45,260
Guess I don't have a choice!

298
00:20:45,260 --> 00:20:47,760
You better not run off with this body!

299
00:20:47,760 --> 00:20:48,760
Cut the jokes!

300
00:20:48,760 --> 00:20:50,060
It's my body to begin with!

301
00:20:50,060 --> 00:20:52,720
Rub a dub dub, thanks for the-

302
00:20:52,720 --> 00:20:53,930
There you are!

303
00:20:58,810 --> 00:21:00,650
Nice one!

304
00:21:00,650 --> 00:21:02,530
I'm glad I picked you, man!

305
00:21:02,530 --> 00:21:03,030
I'm honored!

306
00:21:03,650 --> 00:21:04,610
Is it Lin now?!

307
00:21:04,610 --> 00:21:04,990
Yeah!

308
00:21:05,860 --> 00:21:07,780
You're making me angry...!

309
00:21:07,780 --> 00:21:09,280
And I'm also hungry!

310
00:21:09,280 --> 00:21:12,240
But you guys aren't letting me eat you!

311
00:21:12,700 --> 00:21:13,950
That's why...

312
00:21:13,950 --> 00:21:17,000
...I'm just going to swallow you!

313
00:21:17,290 --> 00:21:18,630
I have a bad feeling!

314
00:21:18,630 --> 00:21:19,750
What do you mean?!

315
00:21:20,000 --> 00:21:21,210
Something's coming.

316
00:21:21,210 --> 00:21:22,630
What , exactly?!

317
00:21:22,960 --> 00:21:25,010
This is... just like back then!

318
00:21:25,010 --> 00:21:25,880
Hey... Whoa, whoa!

319
00:21:25,880 --> 00:21:28,010
What do you guys see that I don't?!

320
00:21:28,010 --> 00:21:30,390
I'm just a normal guy! Explain it to me!

321
00:21:41,690 --> 00:21:42,570
What was that?!

322
00:21:43,150 --> 00:21:44,070
Stay still!

323
00:21:47,070 --> 00:21:48,990
Is there someone else?!

324
00:21:48,990 --> 00:21:49,660
I have no idea.

325
00:21:50,410 --> 00:21:52,910
I haven't got a clue, but this is...!

326
00:21:53,620 --> 00:21:55,790
I...

327
00:21:57,500 --> 00:22:00,830
I know this smell...!

328
00:22:20,440 --> 00:22:21,980
Glad to see you're in top shape!

329
00:22:23,020 --> 00:22:25,570
I've been waiting for you, Lan Fan!

330
00:22:41,250 --> 00:22:46,210
The promise we never made

331
00:22:41,250 --> 00:22:46,210
Kawashita hazu no nai yakasoku ga

332
00:22:46,210 --> 00:22:47,010
yet again

333
00:22:46,210 --> 00:22:47,010
Kyou mo

334
00:22:47,010 --> 00:22:51,840
tries to snatch our future away from us.

335
00:22:47,010 --> 00:22:51,840
Bokura no mirai wo ubaou to suru

336
00:22:53,470 --> 00:22:57,430
Why is it that we can't rejoice

337
00:22:53,470 --> 00:22:57,430
Hoshigatteita mono wo te ni shitemo

338
00:22:57,430 --> 00:22:58,430
straight from the heart

339
00:22:57,430 --> 00:22:58,430
Sunao ni

340
00:22:58,430 --> 00:23:03,400
when we obtain something we've always been after?

341
00:22:58,430 --> 00:23:03,400
Umaku waraenai nowa nazedarou

342
00:23:04,060 --> 00:23:09,110
The overflowing tears aren't from feebleness or remorse.

343
00:23:04,060 --> 00:23:09,110
Afureru namida wo yowasa ya koukai ja nai

344
00:23:09,780 --> 00:23:13,910
They're fragments born from agony.

345
00:23:09,780 --> 00:23:13,910
Itami ga unda kakera de

346
00:23:15,580 --> 00:23:18,950
Of all the moments and destinies,

347
00:23:15,580 --> 00:23:18,950
Donna shunkan datte unmei datte

348
00:23:18,950 --> 00:23:27,710
I realized there's one absolute certainty.

349
00:23:18,950 --> 00:23:27,710
Hitotsu dake tashika na mono ga aru to shitta

350
00:23:27,710 --> 00:23:30,260
Even if things get tough and I'm at my limit

351
00:23:27,710 --> 00:23:30,260
Genkai datte konnan datte

352
00:23:30,260 --> 00:23:34,260
I refuse to give up.

353
00:23:30,260 --> 00:23:34,260
Akirametakunaiyo

354
00:23:34,260 --> 00:23:39,140
Please, don't let go.

355
00:23:34,260 --> 00:23:39,140
Konomama hanasanaide

356
00:23:39,140 --> 00:23:46,980
I can feel the warmth of your right hand

357
00:23:39,140 --> 00:23:46,980
Kataku nigirishimeta kimi no migite no nukumori

358
00:23:46,980 --> 00:23:50,650
where it's tightly joined with my left.

359
00:23:46,980 --> 00:23:50,650
Koko ni arukara

360
00:23:59,410 --> 00:24:03,580
If you only feel fear after knowing both the abilities of your enemy and yourself,

361
00:24:03,580 --> 00:24:05,750
flee with your tail between your legs.

362
00:24:06,250 --> 00:24:09,840
However, if you're going to stand firm and fight with a focused mind,

363
00:24:09,840 --> 00:24:12,090
you will definitely have victory within reach.

364
00:24:13,170 --> 00:24:17,390
Next time, Fullmetal Alchemist:

365
00:24:17,390 --> 00:24:21,390
Episode 48, The Oath in the Tunnel.

366
00:24:17,410 --> 00:24:21,410
The Oath in the Tunnel

367
00:24:21,980 --> 00:24:26,400
Is it right or wrong to achieve victory by sacrificing a fellow comrade?
